From 831289239a718b2a2eac8fd00782968160932005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lane <lane@local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:04:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 16/29] sweep: strip the scratch-path prefix from cpp_reason

Task 2 of 3. sweep.py's cpp_reason recorded the C++ driver's refusal
detail verbatim, but corpus_case.cpp's refusal_record(schema, const
std::exception&) uses error.what() for the "exception" code, and
dsl::DslError (and anything the DSL compiler decorates with a source
location, e.g. EffectRegistry's parameter-validation
std::invalid_argument, rethrown with position context) leads that
string with "<sourceFile>:<line>:<col>: ". Every sweep case's
--source-file is a fresh scratch path, so the report read as a file
path with the real reason buried after it -- 698 cases across ~39
effects in the coordinator's last full-catalog sweep.

Fix: _strip_source_location_prefix(detail, source_path) removes
exactly the current job's own source_path prefix (never a guess at
"looks like a path") plus the trailing "<line>:<col>: " it leads,
leaving the compiler's real message. _cpp_detail() now takes
source_path and applies the strip to both the JSON-parsed detail and
the raw-stdout fallback.

Verification:
- Targeted repro: --effects filter/dither --variants 6 (the 3 cases
  from an earlier 167-effect/6-variant sweep that were affected) --
  cpp_reason now reads 'Parameter "palette" is not renderable by the
  authority: ...' instead of the scratch path.
- Full JS-catalog sweep, no --effects filter, --variants 8 --workers 6
  --no-chains (208 effects, 1664 cases, sweep-out/full-catalog-check):
  391 refused cases, 0 remaining with a path-shaped cpp_reason (checked
  both the "exception" code, 273 cases / 36 effects, and the
  GraphErrorCode "7" compile-define-mismatch code, 118 cases / 21
  effects). Every refusal now carries a clean, actionable message, e.g.
  filter/dither -> 'Parameter "palette" is not renderable by the
  authority: only input(0) and monochrome(1) avoid its
  findClosestPaletteColor NaN-corruption bug', or
  synth3d/noise3d -> 'Effect pass "synth3d/noise3d:precompute"
  unavailable: missing_backend_program (synth3d/noise3d:precompute)'.
- ctest (native + Python CLI suites): same two pre-existing failures as
  before this change, both predating this lane's base commit 9edf5fb
  (confirmed via git merge-base --is-ancestor) and unrelated to this
  string-only fix: the stale classic-noise-oracle SHA in
  tests/oracles/classic_noise_expected.inc, and test_render_cli.py's
  test_a_refused_program_exits_nonzero_and_carries_the_executor_reason,
  whose REFUSED_PROGRAM (median radius:3) stopped refusing once
  fdc95ee's all-radii median custom adapter landed -- also before
  9edf5fb, so the test's fixture was already stale at this lane's
  starting point. No new failures.

